            "review_title": "Review at Al Fresco's",
            "review_text": "Peter B\nEllenbrook, Australia164 contributions\n0\nA taste of home\nNov 2024 • Couples\nEven when you travel in another country sampling, all the great native foods, every now, and then you just feel like having something that reminds you of home.\n\nThis was the case of us last night when we spoke to our wink hotel local guide, saying that we were in the mood for something Italian.\n\nWe were directed to Al frescoes.\n\nA quick grab ride.\n\nWe were greeted at the door by a lady who had the biggest smile, and we were directed to our seat.\n\nThe menu had a good range from salads to pasta to pizza,some Korean items, but what caught us was the good old Aussie pub favourites, the chicken, parmi, and the humble cheeseburger.\n\nI was even asked how I would look how I would like the cheeseburger patties cooked - medium or well done, I went with medium rare.\n\nWhile we were waiting for our food to be cooked, we took part in a jug (very aussie ) of Sangria.\n\nThe food arrived hot, my partners parmigiana was the thickest I've seen in a long time but it was perfectly cooked.\n\nThe cheeseburger was so tasty, the juices dripping onto the plate.\n\nThe tastes took us back home just for that evening.\n\nWe finished off with a huge apple crumble and ice cream for her and a chocolate pudding for me.\n\nDid we overdo it?- Definitely. Did we enjoy it ? Yes. Would we go back again? - of course.\n\nNow, it's not the cheapest meal we have done while here but was very nice.\n\nIf you are after candlelight and romance, then this is not the place for you, but it you are into pizza and pasta plus more, done nicely and quickly. This just might be the place.\nRead more\nWritten November 7, 2024",
